==============================================================================================================
(a) narrow-band limit, symbolic (sympy): radial-offset integral with and without the delta(0) -> T step
==============================================================================================================
   int dE Dm(E)^2 = 2*sigma**3/3  ;  (int dE Dm(E))^2 = sigma**4
   P_tot / (dP/dt)_BO = 2 pi int Dm^2 / (int Dm)^2 = 4*pi/(3*sigma)   (= 4.188790/sigma)
   int dE Dm e^(iEt) e^(-2iwt) = 2*(1 - cos(sigma*t))/t**2  (= sg^2 sinc^2(sg t/2))
   int sinc^4(x) dx = 2*pi/3  -> int R dt / R(0) = (2/sigma) x 2*pi/3 = 4*pi/3/sigma
   R(0) = (dP/dt)_BO = 3/(25*pi) G^2 N^2 w^3 sig^2   (B&O eq. 8: 3/(25 pi) = 0.03819719)
   P_tot = R(0) x 4 pi/(3 sig) = 4/25 G^2 N^2 w^3 sig = 0.160000 G^2 N^2 w^3 sig   [pairs; photons x2]

==============================================================================================================
(b) 'duration' conventions: P_tot vs (dP/dt)_BO x T
==============================================================================================================
   T_eff = P_tot/(dP/dt)_BO = 4 pi/(3 sig) = 4.18879/sig
   T =  1.0000/sig (B&O 'T ~ 1/sigma'):  P_tot / [(dP/dt)_BO x T] = 4.1888
   T =  4.0076/sig (FWHM of R(t) = R(0) sinc^4(sig t/2)):  P_tot / [(dP/dt)_BO x T] = 1.0452
   T =  6.2832/sig (equivalent width of the field intensity sinc^2(sig u/2) at a point = 2 pi/sig):  P_tot / [(dP/dt)_BO x T] = 0.6667
   T =  5.5662/sig (FWHM of the field intensity sinc^2(sig u/2)):  P_tot / [(dP/dt)_BO x T] = 0.7525

